sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Modern as "modern_saas (Postgres)"
    participant Poller as "Poller/Webhook Receiver"
    participant Mapper as "Mapping Engine (YAML v1)"
    participant Resolver as "Conflict Resolver"
    participant Legacy as "legacy_erp (ugly Postgres)"
    participant Audit as "audit_log + DLQ"
    participant Admin as "FastAPI Admin API/UI"

    User->>Modern: UPDATE customer (email changed)
    Modern->>Poller: CDC trigger / webhook
    Poller->>Mapper: normalize record
    Mapper->>Resolver: check for concurrent legacy change
    alt Conflict (clock skew or overlapping update)
        Resolver->>Admin: queue in conflicts table (manual_review)
        Admin->>User: GET /api/conflicts
        User->>Admin: POST /resolve {chosen_state}
        Admin->>Resolver: apply chosen + log
    else No conflict (last-write-wins)
        Resolver->>Legacy: apply mapped upsert (idempotent)
        Legacy->>Audit: record before/after
    end

    Note over Modern,Legacy: Reverse direction works identically via legacy CHANGE_LOG + webhook
    Note over Mapper: Bidirectional transforms, type casts, versioned configs
    Note right of Audit: Every event immutable; dead_letter on poison records after 5 retries

    User->>Admin: docker compose up --build --wait
    Admin->>User: "Sync engine ready. Seeded dirty data with overlapping customer record."
